{"type": "response", "step": 3, "latency_s": 7.1251, "message": {"id": "msg_011CgmFhv3sgRvWAQYhqDj1s", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I didn't expire any snapshots on `db.orders`. The lakehouse's retention policy blocked the request and nothing was changed.\n\n**Why it was blocked:**\n- The policy requires keeping at least the 5 newest snapshots. Keeping only the current one goes below that.\n- Expiring snapshots needs an explicit cutoff timestamp so retention can be checked. Picking out specific snapshots isn't allowed.\n- Expiring is permanent: it removes the history used for rollback and querying past versions.\n\n**Current state:** The table has 8 snapshots, from 100001 (2026-07-07) to 100008 (2026-11-03, current), and 200 rows.\n\n**The most the policy allows:** expiring snapshots older than a cutoff date while keeping the newest 5. That would remove only 100001–100003 (July to early September). I haven't done this because it's not what you asked for. Tell me if you want it.\n\n**On the slowness:** removing old snapshots mostly trims table history and frees storage. It's unlikely to speed up queries much, especially for a 200-row table. Several small appends can leave many small data files, and if that's the cause, combining them into fewer files would help more. I can check the table's file layout or query patterns if you'd like. If you really need only the current snapshot kept, someone who manages the retention policy would have to approve an exception.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1680, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1104, "output_tokens": 563, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 123}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
